{{- define "await-verdict-loop" -}}
- {{binaryName}} await-verdict — Block until review verdict arrives (call after submit-for-review; budget-aware)
  {{binaryName}} await-verdict {{.TaskID}} --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json
  Blocks ~100s per call. Handle the response status:
  - POLL: call await-verdict again in the foreground, using returned timeout_seconds
  - REJECTED: read rejection reason, fix, resubmit
  - APPROVED, TERMINAL, or ALREADY_TRANSITIONED with safe_action=stop: exit normally
  - NEW_ATTEMPT, TIMEOUT, ABORTED: exit normally
  - Budget error: exit normally
  BUDGET: Call await-verdict at most 3 times. If no verdict after 3 calls, exit normally — the supervisor will restart you with the verdict.
  If the harness backgrounds await-verdict and says it will notify on completion, end the turn; do NOT call Monitor, search for Monitor, ScheduleWakeup, or read/tail/sleep/poll the output file.
  Do NOT poll {{binaryName}} get, cat /tmp, or any other command to check for verdict arrival between calls.
  Do NOT wrap in custom polling or background execution; await-verdict is the sole polling primitive.
  Do NOT run more worktree commands after APPROVED, TERMINAL, or ALREADY_TRANSITIONED with safe_action=stop; {{brandTitle}} may already have merged the task and cleaned up the worktree.
{{- end -}}
